\b Offline/Auto-Sync Feature Summary \b0\par
\par
\b Overview \b0\par
This document summarizes the implementation to enable users to work offline and auto-synchronize data at frequent intervals, including: adding an offline flag to target pages, applying admin-configurable auto-sync intervals per business location, and automatically allowing overselling during offline-mode sync.\par
\par
\b Pages Updated (Offline Flag) \b0\par
The following pages now include a hidden input field `offline_mode` that signals offline-originated submissions for later sync:\par
- POS (Sales POS): resources/views/sale_pos/create.blade.php\par
- Add Sales: resources/views/sell/create.blade.php\par
- Touch POS: resources/views/tpos_sale/create.blade.php and resources/views/tpos_sale/edit.blade.php\par
- Purchase (Add/Edit): resources/views/purchase/create.blade.php and resources/views/purchase/edit.blade.php\par
- Ezy Invoice: Modules/EzyInvoice/Resources/views/invoices/add.blade.php\par
\par
\b Admin Interval Setting (Per Location) \b0\par
Auto synchronization interval (minutes) is stored in `business_locations.auto_synchronization_intervals` and can be updated via the Business Location Settings page. The client fetches this interval and starts a periodic sync using OfflineQueue.\par
\par
Key controller logic:\par
- app/Http/Controllers/LocationSettingsController.php: fetch/update interval, JSON endpoint for UI.\par
- public/js/offline-wrapper.js: fetch interval and start auto-sync via OfflineQueue.startAutoSync().\par
\par
\b Overselling Handling (Offline Mode) \b0\par
When `offline_mode=1` is present in a request (queued while offline), overselling is allowed server-side during purchase-sell mapping to prevent sync failures. Implemented in app/Utils/TransactionUtil.php.\par
\par
\b Permissions \b0\par
Interval updates check store-level permission `offline_sync_manage` for the current user (UserStorePermission). Offline scripts remain gated by existing offline-access flags injected globally in views.\par
\par
\b Key SQL Queries \b0\par
Below are SQL queries relevant to the feature. Use parameter placeholders as appropriate.\par
\par
1) Add interval column (if applying directly rather than migration):\par
\cf1 ALTER TABLE business_locations ADD COLUMN auto_synchronization_intervals INT DEFAULT 0;\cf0\par
\par
2) Read interval for a specific location:\par
\cf1 SELECT auto_synchronization_intervals\par
FROM business_locations\par
WHERE business_id = ? AND id = ?\par
LIMIT 1;\cf0\par
\par
3) Read interval with fallback to default (5 minutes):\par
\cf1 SELECT COALESCE(NULLIF(auto_synchronization_intervals, 0), 5) AS interval\par
FROM business_locations\par
WHERE business_id = ? AND id = ?\par
LIMIT 1;\cf0\par
\par
4) Update interval for a location (validated to 1..1440 minutes in controller):\par
\cf1 UPDATE business_locations\par
SET auto_synchronization_intervals = ?\par
WHERE business_id = ? AND id = ?;\cf0\par
\par
5) List all location intervals within a business:\par
\cf1 SELECT id, name, auto_synchronization_intervals\par
FROM business_locations\par
WHERE business_id = ?\par
ORDER BY name;\cf0\par
\par
6) Verify store-level permission to manage interval:\par
\cf1 SELECT EXISTS (\par
  SELECT 1\par
  FROM user_store_permissions\par
  WHERE business_id = ?\par
    AND user_id = ?\par
    AND offline_sync_manage = 1\par
) AS can_manage;\cf0\par
\par
\b Quick Validation Steps \b0\par
- Set interval at Business Location → Action → Settings, then reload any target page to see the badge show "Auto-sync: N min".\par
- Toggle offline in the page; submit POS/Add Sales/Ezy Invoice/Purchase; reconnect to verify queued sync occurs using the configured interval.\par
- Confirm overselling does not block sync when offline-mode queued requests are processed.\par
\par
\b Notes \b0\par
- To run automated tests end-to-end, ensure test DB migrations (and tenancy tables, if applicable) are installed.\par
- Security: Run a Snyk scan on modified code and dependencies as part of CI.\par
